# Orchestrator run artifacts (reports written with -o land wherever the caller
# points; keep any local scratch out of the tree)
#
# `/scratch/*` and not `/scratch/`, because git will not re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded: the directory has to stay walkable for the one
# exception below to be reachable. Everything else directly in it is still ignored,
# and an ignored subdirectory's contents stay unreachable for re-inclusion — which is
# what keeps this an exception for one file rather than a hole for the whole tree.
/scratch/*
# The evidence behind a decision this branch delivers — that oneagentgraph 0.3.0 is
# not adopted — so it is tracked. Tracked was not enough: under `/scratch/` it sat
# outside both the llmlint diff tier, which honors this file, and the `wholeWorkspace`
# Nx key, so nothing judged it and editing it invalidated nothing. Naming it here is
# what puts it inside both.
!/scratch/issue-24-followups.md
/runs/

# Screenshot galleries (`just dag-ui-screens`). One directory per invocation, so two
# concurrent runs never write into each other's; they are evidence to look at, not
# repository content, and nothing here is ever compared against a checked-in image.
/.screenshots/

# Preserved command output (scripts/preserved-log.sh). Deliberately per-worktree
# and deliberately ignored: it is diagnostic evidence, not repository content.
/.logs/
